1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Turn PDFs and scans into structured Excel, with source evidence and a recorded review decision.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Local AI works without a key or per-page API charges. Optional Gemini independently checks difficult pages after explicit cloud authorization.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:29,000
The native invoice PDF becomes one 12-column table across three pages. All 31 rows and the original total are retained.

4
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Selecting invoice row 12 opens page two and highlights its original location. Every exported row retains its source reference.

5
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:48,000
The inventory PDF has no embedded text. Local English OCR reconstructs 20 rows and 12 columns across both scanned pages.

6
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:56,000
This PNG input yields 10 rows and 12 columns. Its 120 data cells and all 12 headers match the fictional source.

7
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:07,000
A fresh 50-page run preserves 500 rows and 12 columns. It removes 49 repeated headers and flags 490 duplicate rows without deleting them.

8
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:14,000
All 500 rows retain source evidence. Page coverage exposes missing table pages. OCR confidence is shown separately.

9
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Nested line items retain header paths and shared order IDs. Inherited values keep their source geometry and remain flagged for review.

10
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:36,000
A description continues on page two. The joined table keeps six rows and 12 columns, with both source parts available for inspection.

11
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:47,000
The deliberately faulty bank statement triggers missing values, balance errors and a total mismatch: stated 2,600 versus a 2,500 row sum.

12
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:56,000
An explicit correction preserves the previous value, records the change and reruns validation. Later edits invalidate any earlier review decision.

13
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Extraction completes as a draft. Review records source checks and requires a note for acknowledged findings, tied to the current data snapshot.

14
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:14,000
The export clearly distinguishes draft and reviewed states. Accepted findings remain visible alongside data, evidence, corrections, coverage and the run log.

15
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:24,000
This is a rendered range from the submitted invoice XLSX: twelve aligned columns, preserved identifiers, typed numbers, dates and percentages.

16
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:35,000
The recorded recovery run resumes a verified completed page, then extracts the next page. Checkpoints must match the source, configuration and engine.

17
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:48,000
Recorded live test: local OCR retains all 20 rows. Gemini checks one scanned page; the one-request cap skips page two. Usage stays visible.

18
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Cloud candidates remain separate for review. Three dummy first-page checks matched 360 cells; two earlier HTTP 503 failures retained the local results.

19
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:09,000
The three submission samples match 864 of 864 data cells. Separate development cohorts cover 16 complex cases and 15 varied layouts.

20
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:19,000
Expanded public and scan checks pass 10 of 11 strict cases. One Sl./SI. header ambiguity is flagged. Development results do not establish hidden-PDF accuracy.

21
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:29,000
The published CI run passed 158 tests on each of Windows, Ubuntu and macOS, plus static quality gates and a non-root Docker conversion check.

22
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Install Python 3.12, extract the full project and double-click START_DAMNLENS.cmd. Bundled models run locally after the first dependency installation.

23
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:45,000
Source, launchers, three PDF–Excel pairs, accuracy reports and this demo are included in the repository and submission ZIP.

24
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Source-linked extraction, explicit validation, optional Gemini review and reproducible checks address all five judging categories.
